From 680d5e7bf1fa2e55a0b15681bfe8500001018eac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vasiliy Yorkin <vasiliy.yorkin@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 15:04:53 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat: route direct keybindings by what the pane runs

A direct (prefix-free) binding belongs to Herdr, so the program inside the
pane never sees that chord. Once a user maps ctrl+h/j/k/l for pane focus,
full-screen editors and pagers lose those chords themselves, and Herdr had
no way to hand one back the way tmux's @pane-is-vim does.

Add keys.direct_keys: "herdr" keeps every direct binding, which is the
default and leaves existing configs alone; "auto" forwards them to the pane
while its application is on the alternate screen, which is what editors and
pagers use; "pane" always forwards them. The client decides per keypress, so
a pane that enters or leaves the alternate screen switches over on the next
chord without a reload. Prefix mode is unaffected.
